.TH "josh" "1" "2026-08-17"
.PP
.SH NAME
.PP
josh - JavaScript Object Shell
.PP
.SH SYNOPSIS
.PP
\fBjosh\fR [--no-config]
.PP
\fBjosh\fR [--no-config] -c <source>
.PP
\fBjosh\fR [--no-config] <script.\&josh>
.PP
\fBjosh\fR -h | --help
.PP
\fBjosh\fR -V | --version
.PP
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
Josh is a Unix-first shell built around structured data.\& Command pipelines carry
bytes on Unix pipes by default; explicit stages (\fItext\fR, \fIjson\fR, \fIlines\fR,
\fIjsonl\fR, \fIchunks\fR, \fImap\fR, \fIfilter\fR, \fItake\fR, \fItakeLast\fR, \fIfirst\fR, \fIcollect\fR)
convert between bytes and typed values.\& Values include booleans, Int, Float,
String, Bytes, Array, Object, Function, Error, and Status, with JavaScript-flavored
prototypes and namespaces (\fIObject\fR, \fIString\fR, \fINumber\fR, \fIBoolean\fR, \fIArray\fR,
\fIFunction\fR, \fIDate\fR, \fIFile\fR, \fIMath\fR).\&
.PP
The scripting language is a strict JavaScript-shaped subset: \fIlet\fR bindings,
\fIfn\fR declarations and arrow closures, destructuring, \fIif\fR/\fIwhile\fR/\fIloop\fR/
\fItry\fR control flow, structured \fIthrow\fR/\fIcatch\fR errors with typed kinds, range
slices (\fIa[b.\&.\&c]\fR) on arrays and strings, and \fIsource f.\&josh\fR for explicitly
including other scripts.\& There is deliberately no \fIfor\fR loop, no \fI==\fR coercing
equality, no \fI++/--\fR, and no background jobs, job control, or module system;
\fIimport\fR/\fIexport\fR are rejected.\&
.PP
For the full language reference see the mdBook manual in \fIdocs/\fR of the
source tree (\fImdbook serve docs\fR) or the rendered copy committed at
\fIdocs/book/index.\&html\fR.\&
.PP
.SH OPTIONS
.PP
\fB--no-config\fR
.RS 4
Skip the \fIenv.\&josh\fR and interactive \fIinit.\&josh\fR startup files.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB-h\fR, \fB--help\fR
.RS 4
Show help and exit 0 without loading config.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB-V\fR, \fB--version\fR
.RS 4
Show the version and exit 0 without loading config.\&
.PP
.RE
.SH INVOCATION
.PP
\fBjosh\fR
.RS 4
Run startup files and start the interactive REPL (Reedline editor, token
highlighting, prefix hints, completion).\&
.PP
.RE
\fBjosh -c SOURCE\fR
.RS 4
Run startup environment, then evaluate one source argument and exit.\&
.PP
.RE
\fBjosh PATH\fR
.RS 4
Run startup environment, then evaluate one UTF-8 script file and exit.\&
.PP
.RE
Neither \fI-c\fR nor script mode accepts trailing positional arguments.\&
.PP
.SH FILES
.PP
\fB$XDG_CONFIG_HOME/josh/env.\&josh\fR, otherwise \fB$HOME/.\&config/josh/env.\&josh\fR
.RS 4
Startup file for every batch, script, and interactive session.\& Runs in the
same global lexical scope as the session; may use \fIsource\fR for includes.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB<config-root>/josh/init.\&josh\fR
.RS 4
Second startup file, interactive sessions only.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB$HOME/.\&josh_history\fR
.RS 4
Plain-file interactive history (overridable with \fIJOSH_HISTORY\fR; falls back
to \fI.\&josh_history\fR in the current directory when HOME is absent).\& Treat it
as sensitive: commands may contain paths or literal data.\&
.PP
.RE
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.PP
\fBXDG_CONFIG_HOME\fR
.RS 4
Selects the config root (see FILES).\& Requires \fIHOME\fR otherwise.\&
.PP
.RE
\fBHOME\fR
.RS 4
Fallback config root plus tilde and history anchoring.\&
.PP
.RE
\fBPATH\fR
.RS 4
Command resolution.\& \fIenv.\&PATH\fR exposes array and scalar views and may be
edited from Josh code; edits persist for the session and its children.\&
.PP
.RE
\fBJOSH_HISTORY\fR
.RS 4
Overrides the history file path.\&
.PP
.RE
.SH EXIT STATUS
.PP
\fB0\fR
.RS 4
Success.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB1\fR
.RS 4
Parse, runtime, or process error in requested source (including \fI-c\fR and
script modes and failed command pipelines).\&
.PP
.RE
\fB2\fR
.RS 4
Usage/read/startup-file errors.\& In batch and script modes a startup-file
error exits 2 before requested source runs; an \fIexit N\fR attempted in a
startup file also exits 2.\&
.PP
.RE
\fBexit N\fR inside requested source returns \fIN\fR.\&
.PP
.SH SEE ALSO
.PP
The Josh manual: \fIdocs/book/index.\&html\fR in the source tree, and the capability
status matrix at \fIdocs/src/status/matrix.\&md\fR, which is the availability
authority.\&
.PP
.SH BUGS
.PP
Known gaps and deliberate exclusions are tracked in the manual'\&s status matrix
and roadmap rather than in bug lists.\&
